gnificant":false,"nucleus_direction":"higher in AD","nucleus_padj":0.746914,"nucleus_log2fc":0.0140963,"nucleus_score":0.497364,"pct_ad":0.370564,"pct_control":0.363929,"donor_test":"not significant","donor_padj":0.999342,"donor_log2fc":-0.0466148,"donor_lfcse":0.0917675,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":-5.71466e-06},{"cell_type":"Oli","gene_symbol":"PDZD8","gene_symbol_current":"PDZD8","gene_id":"ENSG00000165650","nucleus_tested":true,"nucleus_significant":false,"nucleus_direction":"higher in AD","nucleus_padj":0.337258,"nucleus_log2fc":0.0395373,"nucleus_score":1.05548,"pct_ad":0.300731,"pct_control":0.299427,"donor_test":"not significant","donor_padj":0.930331,"donor_log2fc":0.0397682,"donor_lfcse":0.0715109,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":0.00730785}],"modules":[],"degas_bulk_de":false,"drug_target":false}},"description":[{"gene_id":"ENSG00000165650","entrez_id":["118987"],"uniprot":["Q8NEN9"],"ncbi_summary":"Predicted to enable lipid binding activity and metal ion binding activity. Involved in several processes, including mitochondrial calcium ion homeostasis; mitochondrion-endoplasmic reticulum membrane tethering; and regulation of cell morphogenesis. Located in endoplasmic reticulum membrane and mitochondria-associated endoplasmic reticulum membrane. [provided by Alliance of Genome Resources, Apr 2022]","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"Q8NEN9","text":"Lipid transfer and molecular tethering protein, which plays a key role in the formation of membrane contact sites between the endoplasmic reticulum and other organelles, such as late endosomes/lysosomes and mitochondria (PubMed:29097544, PubMed:31636202, PubMed:31818884, PubMed:32686675, PubMed:33912962, PubMed:40246839, PubMed:40839735, PubMed:41512824). Facilitates the exchange of lipids at membrane contact sites between the endoplasmic reticulum and organelles by mediating the transport of lipids, such as ceramide, cholesterol and phosphatidylserine (PubMed:33912962, PubMed:40839735). Also acts as a molecular glue by undergoing liquid-liquid phase separation, forming condensates that mediate stable adhesion between endoplasmic reticulum and surrounding organelles, connecting two distinct membrane-bound vesicles coupled together (PubMed:41512824). Connects the endoplasmic reticulum to late endosomes/lysosomes, facilitating the exchange of lipids, which is crucial for membrane remodeling and processes, such as neurite outgrowth (PubMed:31636202, PubMed:32686675, PubMed:33912962). PDZD8-dependent endoplasmic reticulum-mitochondria membrane tethering is essential for endoplasmic reticulum-mitochondria Ca(2+) transfer (PubMed:29097544, PubMed:31818884, PubMed:40246839). In neurons, involved in the regulation of dendritic Ca(2+) dynamics by regulating mitochondrial Ca(2+) uptake in neurons (PubMed:29097544). Mediates lysosomal vacuolation, a process during which lysosomes abnormally enlarge into large membrane-bound sacs in response to stress such as osmotic stress: acts by mediating bulk lipid transfer from the endoplasmic reticulum to lysosomes, leading to vacuole formation (PubMed:40839735). Plays an indirect role in the regulation of cell morphology and cytoskeletal organization (PubMed:21834987). May indirectly inhibit herpes simplex virus 1 infection at an early stage (PubMed:21549406)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_04","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}